    "notes": [
      "Built against the exact source-equivalent post-Phase-08+09-v3 baseline committed by Devtool as 79df336c; every modified source preimage is SHA-256 pinned.",
      "Corrected replacement for the un-applied Overlay 10 v1; apply v2 directly and do not apply v1 first.",
      "Intermediate campaign overlay: apply with --no-validate; declared Gradle tasks are retained for the final campaign validation gate.",
      "M-031: the real media action preserves the selected variant exact URL/headers and configured destination, evaluates dispatch readiness before mutation, and retains the encrypted/expiry-bounded capture/variant handoff so the same capture can create later outputs.",
      "M-032 app/media side: direct/native/aria2 media is app-owned; yt-dlp/live media is Termux-owned through a real durable post-processing job and never creates a synthetic queued Download.",
      "M-047: Room schema 20 adds media_outputs as one capture to many owner/generation records; migration 19->20 backfills existing capture/download links.",
      "App-owned media_outputs now follow accepted Download retry/completion generations; fresh replacement Download IDs clone the media lineage instead of orphaning it.",
      "A DownloadCreated capture remains reviewable and can create another output generation; secure request handoffs survive successful enqueue until capture removal or expiry.",
      "Download CAS persistence now retains completedArtifactUri, completedArtifactGeneration, and completedArtifactBytes for existing rows so verified completion identity is not discarded.",
      "Library rows are generation-aware. Current app playback is derived only from the validated Download artifact; historical generations do not borrow newer Download state.",
      "Removing an app-owned Library record writes a durable Hidden tombstone for only that generation, preserving the parent capture/file and preventing synchronization resurrection.",
      "Termux terminal/recovery library removal deletes durable job metadata and its output row in one Room transaction; synchronization re-resolves the durable job in-transaction to prevent stale observer resurrection.",
      "M-055 media side: media execution failure categories derive from structured protection/strategy/freshness/DownloadState/BackendType signals; free text is detail rather than classifier authority.",
      "Authenticated Termux session transport remains intentionally held for Overlay 11 rather than placing Cookie/Authorization/Proxy-Authorization or credential-bearing inputs on command lines.",
      "No Gradle compile, unit-test, lint, or project validation tasks were run for this intermediate overlay; targeted Kotlin/static contract, migration/schema, promise, and artifact-integrity checks were performed."
    ]
  },
